<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Saflife yr shr jumps, no div declared.</title>
<headline>Saflife yr shr jumps, no div declared.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre non-recurring   98.8	  vs 72.2</p>
<p>    - post non-recurring  410.2	 vs 72.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs 11.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   157.06	vs 22.44</p>
<p>After tax, pre-recurring income</p>
<p>				  8.37	  vs 4.34</p>
<p>    Non-recurring items   119.99	vs nil</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  28.70	 vs 18.10</p>
<p>Full name: Saflife Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Saflife, the black empowerment firm which recently bought South African mining house JCI Ltd, said that growth potential existed organically and through merger and acquisitions in both the mining and financial service sectors.</p>
<p>Directors said no dividend had been declared so that the firm could utilise its cash flow income to service its debt.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
